On Wed, Mar 31, 2010 at 11:29 AM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote=
:
>=A0One of the really cool things about lojban
> for me is that it is possible (if highly inadvisable) to remove all
> whitespace and still be able to parse the text unambiguously.

Be careful with that claim. It is possible to remove all whitespace,
but you must do TWO things first:

(1) Include all the otherwise optional dots.
(2) Include all the otherwise optional stress marking for brivla.

People tend to remember (1), but sometimes forget (2). You cannot
remove whitespace without including brivla stress marking.

